<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spessart</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spessart is a range of low, densely wooded hills in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, enclosed on three sides by the River Main. For centuries it was a hunting forest of the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, and the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aschaffenburg">Aschaffenburg</a> formed part of their territory. Its oak and beech woods are among the largest continuous forests in Germany.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spessart.jpg" alt="Spessart" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drow69 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rohrberg_Nebel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
